module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.LiftKernel
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SetVariableDerivation
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SquareZeroLiftData

/-! # The divided power polynomial presentation of the colimit of the `ω`-tower

`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/SquareZeroLiftData.lean` builds the algebra
`B` lifting a graded divided power polynomial algebra `A` along a surjection `q : R' → R`, as the
colimit of an `ω`-tower of set-variable divided power extensions. These files equip `B` with a
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedDividedPowerPolynomial` structure. Such a presentation has to
exhibit every finite variable stage spanning *several* degrees as a one-variable extension of its
predecessor, while the set-variable construction states this only within a single degree. With
the presentation, the two clauses of Tag 09PS which need freeness — `mem_ker_iff` and
`kappa_apply`, provided by `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftReduction` from a presentation —
hold for the lift.

Three things have to be built.

*The mapping property, with the target universe free.* The universal property of a stage of the
tower is available only for targets in the *one* universe which was fixed when the stage was
chosen: the target universe is quantified inside the existential of
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.exists_setVariableDividedPowerExtension`, so it occurs in the
universe of the stage. In particular it cannot be applied to an algebra built out of the
colimit's own carrier — which is exactly what the freeness argument needs. The output *shape* of
the construction, recorded as `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSetVariableExtension`, determines
the extension, and the mapping property is proved from the predicate alone with the target
universe free, by the argument
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.existsUnique_gradedDividedPowerPolynomial_map` runs for a graded
divided power polynomial algebra. Assembling the steps along the chain gives the mapping
property of the colimit.

*The finite variable stages as graded divided power subalgebras.* A stage spanning several
degrees is a graded subring, by the same argument as in a single degree — only homogeneity of
each variable is used, not a common degree — and it is closed under divided powers, which is
reduced to the single-degree statement by induction on a bound for the degrees: the variables of
the top degree are adjoined to the subalgebra generated by those of lower degree, which by
induction may serve as the coefficient algebra.

*The successor step.* Adjoining one more variable to such a stage gives exactly the odd or even
one-variable extension. The map out of the one-variable extension comes from the one-variable
mapping properties of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/VariableLift.lean`, its image is the next
stage by a generation argument, and it is injective because the mapping property sends the
colimit back into that one-variable extension, retracting it.

## Main definitions

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsHomogeneousVariableFamily` — the hypotheses under which the
  finite variable stages are graded subrings.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.stageGrade`, `stageDividedPowers`,
  `stageDPAlgebra` — a finite variable stage as a graded divided power algebra.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.HasVariableMappingProperty` — freeness on the coefficients and
  the variables, for targets in the algebra's own universe.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftPresentation` — the presentation of the lifted algebra.

## Main results

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSetVariableExtension.existsUnique_ringHom` — the mapping
  property of a set-variable divided power extension, for a target in an arbitrary universe.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.towerColimit_exists_gradedDPHom` and
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftAlgebra_exists_gradedDPHom` — the same for the colimit of the
  `ω`-tower and for the lifted algebra.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.finiteVariableStage_dpow_mem_of_homogeneous` — a mixed-degree
  finite variable stage is closed under divided powers.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.towerColimit_finite_support` — the finite variable stages cover
  the colimit.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.gradedDividedPowerPolynomialOfMappingProperty` — the presentation
  theorem: a graded divided power algebra generated by degree-zero coefficients and homogeneous
  variables, covered by its finite variable stages and free on that data, is a graded divided
  power polynomial algebra.

## Implementation notes

The colimit's carrier is a *reducible* abbreviation ending in a `DirectLimit`, so instance search
unfolds it and picks up the `DirectLimit` instances rather than the bundle's own; every
unification of a `Subring` of the colimit against a lemma then becomes expensive enough to
exhaust the heartbeat budget. The statements about finite variable stages of the colimit are
therefore proved with the bundle, the family of variables and the index type all abstract, and
instantiated afterwards, which is cheap.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F4I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F4I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PS)

This file holds the first of the three steps, the mapping property; the finite variable stages
are in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/TowerPresentation/MixedStage.lean`,
the successor step and the presentation in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/TowerPresentation/Presentation.lean`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DividedPowers.TateResolution

universe u v w y z

section SetVariableMap

open EvenVariableAlgebra OddVariableExtension

variable {R : Type u} {A : Type v} {C : Type z} {J : Type w} {D : Type y}
  [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring C] [Algebra R C] [Ring D] [Algebra R D]
  {Aᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra Aᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Aᵢ]
  {γ : DividedPowerStructure Aᵢ}
  {Cᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R C} [GradedAlgebra Cᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Cᵢ]
  {δ : DividedPowerStructure Cᵢ} {ι : A →ₐ[R] C} {T : J → C} {d : ℕ} {hd : 0 < d}
  (hC : IsSetVariableExtension Aᵢ γ Cᵢ δ ι T d hd)
  (Dᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R D) [GradedAlgebra Dᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Dᵢ]
  (ε : DividedPowerStructure Dᵢ) (f : A →+* D) (t : J → D)

/-- A ring homomorphism out of a finite variable stage of a set-variable extension realises the
prescribed data: it restricts to `f` on the coefficients, sends each variable of the stage to its
prescribed image, sends the divided powers of a variable to the divided powers of its image when
the degree is even, preserves homogeneous degrees, and is compatible with divided powers. -/
private def IsSetStageLift (S : Finset J) (g : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S →+* D) : Prop :=
  (∀ a : A, g ⟨ι a, mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T S a⟩ = f a) ∧
  (∀ (j : J) (hj : j ∈ S), g ⟨T j, mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T hj⟩ = t j) ∧
  (∀ (j : J) (hj : j ∈ S) (n : ℕ), Even d →
    g ⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T hj n⟩ = ε.dpow n (t j)) ∧
  (∀ (m : ℕ) (x : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S), (x : C) ∈ Cᵢ m → g x ∈ Dᵢ m) ∧
  (∀ (n : ℕ) (x : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S), (x : C) ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ →
    ∀ hmem : δ.dpow n (x : C) ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T S,
      g ⟨δ.dpow n (x : C), hmem⟩ = ε.dpow n (g x))

include hC in
/-- Every divided power of a variable of odd degree is zero or one, so its image under a ring
homomorphism needs no prescribing. -/
private theorem dpow_odd_variable_eq_zero_or_one (hodd : Odd d) (j : J) (n : ℕ) :
    δ.dpow n (T j) = 0 ∨ δ.dpow n (T j) = 1 := by
  by_cases hmem : T j ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ
  · rcases positiveEven_homogeneous_eq_zero_or_grade Cᵢ (hC.generator_mem j) hmem with
      hz | ⟨c, hc⟩
    · by_cases hn : n = 0
      · subst n
        exact Or.inr (by rw [hz]; exact δ.dpow_zero (Submodule.zero_mem _))
      · exact Or.inl (by rw [hz]; exact δ.dpow_zero_eq_zero hn)
    · exact absurd hc (by obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hodd; omega)
  · exact Or.inl (δ.dpow_null hmem)

include hC in
/-- The divided powers of a variable have a forced image under any realisation. -/
private theorem isSetStageLift_dpow_generator_eq {S U : Finset J} (hSU : S ⊆ U)
    {g₁ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S →+* D} {g₂ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T U →+* D}
    (h₁ : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t S g₁) (h₂ : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t U g₂)
    (j : J) (hj : j ∈ S) (n : ℕ) :
    g₁ ⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T hj n⟩ =
      g₂ ⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T (hSU hj) n⟩ := by
  by_cases heven : Even d
  · exact (h₁.2.2.1 j hj n heven).trans (h₂.2.2.1 j (hSU hj) n heven).symm
  · rcases dpow_odd_variable_eq_zero_or_one hC (Nat.not_even_iff_odd.mp heven) j n with hz | ho
    · rw [show (⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T hj n⟩ :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T S) = 0 from Subtype.ext hz,
        show (⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T (hSU hj) n⟩ :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T U) = 0 from Subtype.ext hz, map_zero, map_zero]
    · rw [show (⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T hj n⟩ :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T S) = 1 from Subtype.ext ho,
        show (⟨δ.dpow n (T j), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T (hSU hj) n⟩ :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T U) = 1 from Subtype.ext ho, map_one, map_one]

include hC in
/-- A realisation of the prescribed data on a finite variable stage is unique. -/
private theorem isSetStageLift_unique {S : Finset J}
    {g₁ g₂ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S →+* D}
    (h₁ : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t S g₁)
    (h₂ : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t S g₂) : g₁ = g₂ :=
  finiteVariableStage_ringHom_ext δ ι T S g₁ g₂ (fun a => (h₁.1 a).trans (h₂.1 a).symm)
    (fun j hj => (h₁.2.1 j hj).trans (h₂.2.1 j hj).symm)
    (isSetStageLift_dpow_generator_eq hC Dᵢ ε f t (Finset.Subset.refl S) h₁ h₂)

include hC in
/-- Realisations on nested stages agree wherever both are defined. -/
private theorem isSetStageLift_agree {S U : Finset J} (hSU : S ⊆ U)
    {g₁ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S →+* D} {g₂ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T U →+* D}
    (h₁ : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t S g₁) (h₂ : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t U g₂)
    (x : C) (hx : x ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T S) (hx' : x ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T U) :
    g₁ ⟨x, hx⟩ = g₂ ⟨x, hx'⟩ :=
  finiteVariableStage_ringHom_eq_of_subset δ ι T hSU g₁ g₂
    (fun a => (h₁.1 a).trans (h₂.1 a).symm)
    (fun j hj => (h₁.2.1 j hj).trans (h₂.2.1 j (hSU hj)).symm)
    (isSetStageLift_dpow_generator_eq hC Dᵢ ε f t hSU h₁ h₂) x hx hx'

include hC in
/-- A realisation of the prescribed data exists on every finite variable stage. The empty stage
is the image of the coefficient algebra, on which the degree and divided power clauses hold
because an injective degree-preserving coefficient map *reflects* homogeneous degrees and the
positive even part. Each successor stage is the relevant one-variable extension, across which
the map is extended by the one-variable mapping property. -/
private theorem exists_isSetStageLift
    (hf : ∀ (m : ℕ) (a : A), a ∈ Aᵢ m → f a ∈ Dᵢ m)
    (hfdp : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : A), a ∈ positiveEvenPart Aᵢ → ε.dpow n (f a) = f (γ.dpow n a))
    (ht : ∀ j : J, t j ∈ Dᵢ d) (S : Finset J) :
    ∃ g : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S →+* D, IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t S g := by
  let instDec : DecidableEq J := Classical.decEq _
  refine Finset.induction_on S ?_ ?_
  · have hsurj : ∀ x : C, x ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (∅ : Finset J) → ∃ a : A, ι a = x := by
      intro x hx
      induction hx using Subring.closure_induction with
      | mem y hy =>
          rcases hy with ⟨a, rfl⟩ | ⟨c, hc, -⟩
          · exact ⟨a, rfl⟩
          · exact absurd hc (Finset.notMem_empty c)
      | zero => exact ⟨0, map_zero ι⟩
      | one => exact ⟨1, map_one ι⟩
      | add a b _ _ iha ihb =>
          obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := iha
          obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := ihb
          exact ⟨p + q, by rw [map_add, hp, hq]⟩
      | neg a _ iha =>
          obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := iha
          exact ⟨-p, by rw [map_neg, hp]⟩
      | mul a b _ _ iha ihb =>
          obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := iha
          obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := ihb
          exact ⟨p * q, by rw [map_mul, hp, hq]⟩
    let coeffHom : A →+* finiteVariableStage δ ι T (∅ : Finset J) :=
      { toFun := fun a => ⟨ι a, mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T ∅ a⟩
        map_one' := Subtype.ext (map_one ι)
        map_mul' := fun a b => Subtype.ext (map_mul ι a b)
        map_zero' := Subtype.ext (map_zero ι)
        map_add' := fun a b => Subtype.ext (map_add ι a b) }
    have hbij : Function.Bijective coeffHom :=
      ⟨fun a b hab => hC.coefficient_injective (congrArg Subtype.val hab), fun x =>
        let ⟨a, ha⟩ := hsurj x.1 x.2; ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩⟩
    let coeffEquiv := RingEquiv.ofBijective coeffHom hbij
    have hval : ∀ (a : A) (hx : ι a ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (∅ : Finset J)),
        (f.comp coeffEquiv.symm.toRingHom) ⟨ι a, hx⟩ = f a := fun a _ =>
      congrArg f (coeffEquiv.symm_apply_apply a)
    have hpre : ∀ x : finiteVariableStage δ ι T (∅ : Finset J), ι (coeffEquiv.symm x) = (x : C) :=
      by
      intro x
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hsurj x.1 x.2
      rw [show x = coeffEquiv a from Subtype.ext ha.symm, coeffEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
      exact rfl
    refine ⟨f.comp coeffEquiv.symm.toRingHom, fun a => hval a _,
      fun c hc => absurd hc (Finset.notMem_empty c),
      fun c hc _ _ => absurd hc (Finset.notMem_empty c), ?_, ?_⟩
    · intro m x hx
      have hmem : coeffEquiv.symm x ∈ Aᵢ m :=
        mem_grade_of_map_mem_grade Aᵢ Cᵢ ι hC.coefficient_grade hC.coefficient_injective m
          (by rw [hpre x]; exact hx)
      exact hf m _ hmem
    · intro n x hx hmem
      have hxpos : coeffEquiv.symm x ∈ positiveEvenPart Aᵢ :=
        mem_positiveEvenPart_of_map_mem_positiveEvenPart Aᵢ Cᵢ ι hC.coefficient_grade
          hC.coefficient_injective (by rw [hpre x]; exact hx)
      have hform : δ.dpow n (x : C) = ι (γ.dpow n (coeffEquiv.symm x)) := by
        rw [← hC.coefficient_dpow n _ hxpos, hpre x]
      rw [show (⟨δ.dpow n (x : C), hmem⟩ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T (∅ : Finset J)) =
          coeffEquiv (γ.dpow n (coeffEquiv.symm x)) from Subtype.ext hform]
      show f (coeffEquiv.symm (coeffEquiv (γ.dpow n (coeffEquiv.symm x)))) = _
      rw [coeffEquiv.symm_apply_apply, ← hfdp n _ hxpos]
      rfl
  · intro j S₀ hjS₀ ih
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨aS, Sᵢ, gS, cS, δS, hδ, hoddbr, hevenbr⟩ := hC.successor S₀ j hjS₀
    let := aS
    let := gS
    have key : (∀ (m : ℕ) (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀), b ∈ Sᵢ m ↔ (b : C) ∈ Cᵢ m) →
        (∀ (m : ℕ) (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀), b ∈ Sᵢ m → g b ∈ Dᵢ m) ∧
        ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀),
          b ∈ positiveEvenPart Sᵢ → ε.dpow n (g b) = g (δS.dpow n b) := by
      intro hSmem
      refine ⟨fun m b hb => hg.2.2.2.1 m b ((hSmem m b).mp hb), fun n b hb => ?_⟩
      have hbC : (b : C) ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ := by
        induction hb using Submodule.iSup_induction' with
        | mem k b hbm => exact Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem k ((hSmem _ b).mp hbm)
        | zero => simp
        | add b b' _ _ ihb ihb' => simpa using Submodule.add_mem _ ihb ihb'
      have hmem : δ.dpow n (b : C) ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀ := by
        rw [← hδ n b hb]
        exact (δS.dpow n b).2
      rw [← hg.2.2.2.2 n b hbC hmem]
      exact congrArg g (Subtype.ext (hδ n b hb).symm)
    let := cS
    rcases Nat.even_or_odd d with heven | hodd
    · have instFact : Fact (Even d) := ⟨heven⟩
      obtain ⟨e, he1, he2, he3, he4⟩ := hevenbr heven
      have hSmem : ∀ (m : ℕ) (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀),
          b ∈ Sᵢ m ↔ (b : C) ∈ Cᵢ m := by
        intro m b
        have h1 : EvenVariableAlgebra.coeffEmbedding b ∈
            EvenVariableAlgebra.grade Sᵢ d m ↔ (b : C) ∈ Cᵢ m := by rw [he3, he1]
        rw [← h1, EvenVariableAlgebra.coeffEmbedding_mem_grade_iff]
      obtain ⟨hgS, hdpowS⟩ := key hSmem
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : ∃ c, d = 2 * c := by obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := heven; exact ⟨c, by omega⟩
      have htpos : t j ∈ positiveEvenPart Dᵢ := by
        refine Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (c - 1) ?_
        rw [show 2 * (c - 1 + 1) = d by omega]
        exact ht j
      have hmon1 : EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial 1 (1 : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀) ∈
          positiveEvenPart (EvenVariableAlgebra.grade Sᵢ d) := by
        refine Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (c - 1) ?_
        rw [show 2 * (c - 1 + 1) = 1 * d by omega]
        exact EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial_one_mem_grade Sᵢ d 1
      obtain ⟨k, hk, -⟩ := existsUnique_evenVariableAlgebra_ringHom Sᵢ Dᵢ ε g hgS d hd heven
        (t j) (ht j)
      have hkdpow := evenVariableAlgebra_ringHom_dpow Sᵢ δS Dᵢ ε g hdpowS d hd (t j) (ht j)
        k hk.1 hk.2.1 hk.2.2
      have hextg : ∀ (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀)
          (hb : (b : C) ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)),
          (k.comp e.symm.toRingHom) ⟨(b : C), hb⟩ = g b := by
        intro b hb
        have h1 : (⟨(b : C), hb⟩ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)) =
            e (EvenVariableAlgebra.coeffEmbedding b) := Subtype.ext (he1 b).symm
        show k (e.symm ⟨(b : C), hb⟩) = g b
        rw [h1, e.symm_apply_apply, hk.1]
      have hdpowgen : ∀ n : ℕ, δ.dpow n (T j) =
          ((e (EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial n (1 : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀)) :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)) : C) := by
        intro n
        have h := he4 n (EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial 1 1) hmon1
        rw [he2] at h
        refine h.trans (congrArg
          (fun y => ((e y : finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)) : C)) ?_)
        exact evenVariableDividedPowerStructure_dpow_monomial_one Sᵢ δS d hd n
      refine ⟨k.comp e.symm.toRingHom, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
      · intro a
        exact (hextg ⟨ι a, mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T S₀ a⟩
          (mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T (insert j S₀) a)).trans (hg.1 a)
      · intro j' hj'
        rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hj' with rfl | hj'S
        · rw [show (⟨T j', mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T hj'⟩ :
              finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j' S₀)) =
              e (EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial 1 1) from Subtype.ext he2.symm]
          show k (e.symm (e (EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial 1 1))) = t j'
          rw [e.symm_apply_apply, hk.2.1 1, ε.dpow_one htpos]
        · exact (hextg ⟨T j', mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T hj'S⟩ _).trans
            (hg.2.1 j' hj'S)
      · intro j' hj' n _
        rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hj' with rfl | hj'S
        · rw [show (⟨δ.dpow n (T j'), mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T hj' n⟩ :
              finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j' S₀)) =
              e (EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial n 1) from Subtype.ext (hdpowgen n)]
          show k (e.symm (e (EvenVariableAlgebra.monomial n 1))) = ε.dpow n (t j')
          rw [e.symm_apply_apply, hk.2.1 n]
        · exact (hextg ⟨δ.dpow n (T j'),
            mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T hj'S n⟩ _).trans
            (hg.2.2.1 j' hj'S n heven)
      · intro m x hx
        show k (e.symm x) ∈ Dᵢ m
        refine hk.2.2 m (e.symm x) ?_
        rw [he3 m (e.symm x), e.apply_symm_apply]
        exact hx
      · intro n x hx hmem
        have hy : e.symm x ∈ positiveEvenPart (EvenVariableAlgebra.grade Sᵢ d) :=
          mem_positiveEvenPart_symm_of_ringEquiv Cᵢ (EvenVariableAlgebra.grade Sᵢ d) _ e he3 hx
        have hform := he4 n (e.symm x) hy
        rw [e.apply_symm_apply] at hform
        rw [show (⟨δ.dpow n (x : C), hmem⟩ :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)) =
            e ((evenVariableDividedPowerStructure d hd δS).dpow n (e.symm x))
            from Subtype.ext hform]
        show k (e.symm (e ((evenVariableDividedPowerStructure d hd δS).dpow n
          (e.symm x)))) = ε.dpow n (k (e.symm x))
        rw [e.symm_apply_apply]
        exact (hkdpow n (e.symm x) hy).symm
    · obtain ⟨e, he1, he2, he3, he4⟩ := hoddbr hodd
      have hSmem : ∀ (m : ℕ) (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀),
          b ∈ Sᵢ m ↔ (b : C) ∈ Cᵢ m := by
        intro m b
        have h1 : OddVariableExtension.inclusion Sᵢ d b ∈
            OddVariableExtension.grade Sᵢ d m ↔ (b : C) ∈ Cᵢ m := by rw [he3, he1]
        rw [← h1]
        refine ⟨fun hb => OddVariableExtension.inclusion_mem_grade Sᵢ d m hb, fun hb => ?_⟩
        rw [OddVariableExtension.mem_grade_iff] at hb
        exact hb.1
      obtain ⟨hgS, hdpowS⟩ := key hSmem
      obtain ⟨k, hk, -⟩ := existsUnique_oddVariableExtension_ringHom Sᵢ Dᵢ g hgS d hodd
        (t j) (ht j)
      have hkdpow := oddVariableExtension_ringHom_dpow Sᵢ δS Dᵢ ε g hgS hdpowS d hd hodd
        (t j) (ht j) k hk.1 hk.2.1
      have hextg : ∀ (b : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S₀)
          (hb : (b : C) ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)),
          (k.comp e.symm.toRingHom) ⟨(b : C), hb⟩ = g b := by
        intro b hb
        have h1 : (⟨(b : C), hb⟩ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)) =
            e (OddVariableExtension.inclusion Sᵢ d b) := Subtype.ext (he1 b).symm
        show k (e.symm ⟨(b : C), hb⟩) = g b
        rw [h1, e.symm_apply_apply, hk.1]
      refine ⟨k.comp e.symm.toRingHom, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
      · intro a
        exact (hextg ⟨ι a, mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T S₀ a⟩
          (mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T (insert j S₀) a)).trans (hg.1 a)
      · intro j' hj'
        rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hj' with rfl | hj'S
        · rw [show (⟨T j', mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T hj'⟩ :
              finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j' S₀)) =
              e (OddVariableExtension.generator Sᵢ d) from Subtype.ext he2.symm]
          show k (e.symm (e (OddVariableExtension.generator Sᵢ d))) = t j'
          rw [e.symm_apply_apply, hk.2.1]
        · exact (hextg ⟨T j', mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T hj'S⟩ _).trans
            (hg.2.1 j' hj'S)
      · intro j' hj' n heven'
        exact absurd heven' (Nat.not_even_iff_odd.mpr hodd)
      · intro m x hx
        show k (e.symm x) ∈ Dᵢ m
        refine hk.2.2 m (e.symm x) ?_
        rw [he3 m (e.symm x), e.apply_symm_apply]
        exact hx
      · intro n x hx hmem
        have hy : e.symm x ∈ positiveEvenPart (OddVariableExtension.grade Sᵢ d) :=
          mem_positiveEvenPart_symm_of_ringEquiv Cᵢ (OddVariableExtension.grade Sᵢ d) _ e he3 hx
        have hform := he4 n (e.symm x) hy
        rw [e.apply_symm_apply] at hform
        rw [show (⟨δ.dpow n (x : C), hmem⟩ :
            finiteVariableStage δ ι T (insert j S₀)) =
            e ((oddVariableDividedPowerStructure Sᵢ δS d hd hodd).dpow n (e.symm x))
            from Subtype.ext hform]
        show k (e.symm (e ((oddVariableDividedPowerStructure Sᵢ δS d hd hodd).dpow n
          (e.symm x)))) = ε.dpow n (k (e.symm x))
        rw [e.symm_apply_apply]
        exact (hkdpow n (e.symm x) hy).symm

include hC in
/-- **The mapping property of a set-variable divided power extension, with the target universe
free.** A ring homomorphism out of the extension is determined by, and may be prescribed by, its
restriction to the coefficient algebra together with a homogeneous image of degree `d` for each
adjoined variable; the prescribed restriction has to preserve homogeneous degrees and divided
powers, and the resulting map does so too.

This is the universal property of
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.exists_setVariableExtension_bundled` freed of its universe
restriction: that statement quantifies over targets in one fixed universe, because the extension
is *chosen* from an existential in which the target universe occurs, while the predicate
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSetVariableExtension` recorded here determines the extension and
lets the property be proved for a target anywhere. -/
public theorem IsSetVariableExtension.existsUnique_ringHom
    (hf : ∀ (m : ℕ) (a : A), a ∈ Aᵢ m → f a ∈ Dᵢ m)
    (hfdp : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : A), a ∈ positiveEvenPart Aᵢ → ε.dpow n (f a) = f (γ.dpow n a))
    (ht : ∀ j : J, t j ∈ Dᵢ d) :
    ∃! G : C →+* D,
      (∀ a : A, G (ι a) = f a) ∧ (∀ j : J, G (T j) = t j) ∧
      (∀ (m : ℕ) (x : C), x ∈ Cᵢ m → G x ∈ Dᵢ m) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (x : C), x ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ → ε.dpow n (G x) = G (δ.dpow n x)) := by
  classical
  choose gS hgS using exists_isSetStageLift hC Dᵢ ε f t hf hfdp ht
  have hcompat : ∀ (S U : Finset J) (x : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S)
      (y : finiteVariableStage δ ι T U), (x : C) = (y : C) → gS S x = gS U y := by
    intro S U x y hxy
    have hxu : (x : C) ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (S ∪ U) :=
      finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_left x.2
    have hyu : (y : C) ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (S ∪ U) :=
      finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_right y.2
    rw [isSetStageLift_agree hC Dᵢ ε f t Finset.subset_union_left (hgS S) (hgS (S ∪ U))
        (x : C) x.2 hxu,
      isSetStageLift_agree hC Dᵢ ε f t Finset.subset_union_right (hgS U) (hgS (S ∪ U))
        (y : C) y.2 hyu]
    exact congrArg (gS (S ∪ U)) (Subtype.ext hxy)
  obtain ⟨G, hG, hGuniq⟩ :=
    finiteVariableStages_directedColimit Cᵢ δ ι T hC.finite_support gS hcompat
  have hGcoeff : ∀ a : A, G (ι a) = f a := by
    intro a
    rw [hG ∅ ⟨ι a, mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T ∅ a⟩]
    exact (hgS ∅).1 a
  have hGgen : ∀ j : J, G (T j) = t j := by
    intro j
    rw [hG {j} ⟨T j, mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T (Finset.mem_singleton_self j)⟩]
    exact (hgS {j}).2.1 j (Finset.mem_singleton_self j)
  have hGgrade : ∀ (m : ℕ) (x : C), x ∈ Cᵢ m → G x ∈ Dᵢ m := by
    intro m x hx
    obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := hC.finite_support x
    rw [hG S ⟨x, hS⟩]
    exact (hgS S).2.2.2.1 m ⟨x, hS⟩ hx
  have hGdpow : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : C), x ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ →
      ε.dpow n (G x) = G (δ.dpow n x) := by
    intro n x hx
    obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := hC.finite_support x
    obtain ⟨S', hS'⟩ := hC.finite_support (δ.dpow n x)
    have hxV : x ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (S ∪ S') :=
      finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_left hS
    have hdV : δ.dpow n x ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T (S ∪ S') :=
      finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_right hS'
    rw [hG (S ∪ S') ⟨δ.dpow n x, hdV⟩, hG (S ∪ S') ⟨x, hxV⟩]
    exact ((hgS (S ∪ S')).2.2.2.2 n ⟨x, hxV⟩ hx hdV).symm
  refine ⟨G, ⟨hGcoeff, hGgen, hGgrade, hGdpow⟩, ?_⟩
  intro g' hg'
  refine hGuniq g' ?_
  intro S x
  have hstage : IsSetStageLift (d := d) Dᵢ ε f t S
      (g'.comp (finiteVariableStage δ ι T S).subtype) := by
    refine ⟨fun a => hg'.1 a, fun j _ => hg'.2.1 j, fun j _ n heven => ?_,
      fun m y hy => hg'.2.2.1 m (y : C) hy, fun n y hy _ => (hg'.2.2.2 n (y : C) hy).symm⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : ∃ c, d = 2 * c := by obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := heven; exact ⟨c, by omega⟩
    have hgenpos : T j ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ := by
      refine mem_positiveEvenPart_of_mem_grade Cᵢ (d := c) (by omega) ?_
      rw [← hc]
      exact hC.generator_mem j
    show g' (δ.dpow n (T j)) = ε.dpow n (t j)
    rw [← hg'.2.2.2 n (T j) hgenpos, hg'.2.1 j]
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun (isSetStageLift_unique hC Dᵢ ε f t hstage (hgS S)) x

end SetVariableMap

section StageUnion

variable {R : Type u} {P : Type v} {C : Type z} {J : Type w}
  [CommRing R] [Ring P] [Algebra R P] [Ring C] [Algebra R C]
  {Cᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R C} [GradedAlgebra Cᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Cᵢ]
  (δ : DividedPowerStructure Cᵢ) (ι : P →ₐ[R] C) (T : J → C)

/-- The union of the finite variable stages, as a subring: the stages are directed, so their
union is closed under the ring operations. -/
public def variableStageUnion : Subring C where
  carrier := {y | ∃ S : Finset J, y ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T S}
  zero_mem' := ⟨∅, Subring.zero_mem _⟩
  one_mem' := ⟨∅, Subring.one_mem _⟩
  add_mem' := by
    classical
    rintro a b ⟨S, hS⟩ ⟨U, hU⟩
    exact ⟨S ∪ U, Subring.add_mem _
      (finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_left hS)
      (finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_right hU)⟩
  neg_mem' := by
    rintro a ⟨S, hS⟩
    exact ⟨S, Subring.neg_mem _ hS⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    classical
    rintro a b ⟨S, hS⟩ ⟨U, hU⟩
    exact ⟨S ∪ U, Subring.mul_mem _
      (finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_left hS)
      (finiteVariableStage_le_of_subset δ ι T Finset.subset_union_right hU)⟩

/-- Membership in the union of the finite variable stages. -/
@[simp]
public theorem mem_variableStageUnion {y : C} :
    y ∈ variableStageUnion δ ι T ↔ ∃ S : Finset J, y ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T S := Iff.rfl

/-- A finite variable stage depends on the coefficient map only through its image. -/
public theorem finiteVariableStage_congr_coefficient {P' : Type*} [Ring P'] [Algebra R P']
    (ι' : P' →ₐ[R] C) (hrange : Set.range ι' = Set.range ι) (S : Finset J) :
    finiteVariableStage δ ι' T S = finiteVariableStage δ ι T S := by
  unfold finiteVariableStage
  rw [hrange]

/-- A coefficient lies in the union of the finite variable stages. -/
public theorem coefficient_mem_variableStageUnion (p : P) :
    ι p ∈ variableStageUnion δ ι T :=
  ⟨∅, mem_finiteVariableStage_coefficient δ ι T ∅ p⟩

/-- A variable lies in the union of the finite variable stages. -/
public theorem generator_mem_variableStageUnion (j : J) :
    T j ∈ variableStageUnion δ ι T :=
  ⟨{j}, mem_finiteVariableStage_generator δ ι T (Finset.mem_singleton_self j)⟩

/-- A divided power of a variable lies in the union of the finite variable stages. -/
public theorem dpow_generator_mem_variableStageUnion (j : J) (n : ℕ) :
    δ.dpow n (T j) ∈ variableStageUnion δ ι T :=
  ⟨{j}, mem_finiteVariableStage_dpow_generator δ ι T (Finset.mem_singleton_self j) n⟩

/-- A homomorphism maps a finite variable stage into any subring of the target containing the
images of the coefficients, of the variables of the stage, and of their divided powers. -/
public theorem finiteVariableStage_map_mem_subring {D : Type y} [Ring D] [Algebra R D]
    (S : Finset J) (f : C →ₐ[R] D) (W : Subring D) (hcoeff : ∀ p : P, f (ι p) ∈ W)
    (hgen : ∀ j ∈ S, f (T j) ∈ W) (hdpow : ∀ j ∈ S, ∀ n : ℕ, f (δ.dpow n (T j)) ∈ W)
    {x : C} (hx : x ∈ finiteVariableStage δ ι T S) : f x ∈ W := by
  refine (?_ : finiteVariableStage δ ι T S ≤ Subring.comap f.toRingHom W) hx
  refine Subring.closure_le.2 ?_
  rintro z (⟨p, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, hj, rfl | ⟨n, rfl⟩⟩)
  · exact hcoeff p
  · exact hgen j hj
  · exact hdpow j hj n

/-- **The image of a set-variable extension lands in any subring of the target containing the
images of the coefficients, of the variables, and of their divided powers.** Stated with every
piece abstract, so that it may be instantiated at a stage of the `ω`-tower without the elaborator
having to unify the stage's own structures. -/
public theorem setVariableExtension_map_mem_subring {A : Type v} {D : Type y}
    [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring D] [Algebra R D]
    {Aᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra Aᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Aᵢ]
    {γ : DividedPowerStructure Aᵢ} {ι' : A →ₐ[R] C} {d : ℕ} {hd : 0 < d}
    (hC : IsSetVariableExtension Aᵢ γ Cᵢ δ ι' T d hd)
    (Dᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R D) [GradedAlgebra Dᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Dᵢ]
    (ε : DividedPowerStructure Dᵢ) (W : Subring D) (g : C →ₐ[R] D)
    (hgdpow : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : C), a ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ → ε.dpow n (g a) = g (δ.dpow n a))
    (hcoeff : ∀ a : A, g (ι' a) ∈ W) (hgen : ∀ j : J, g (T j) ∈ W)
    (hdpowgen : ∀ (j : J) (n : ℕ), ε.dpow n (g (T j)) ∈ W) (y : C) : g y ∈ W := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := hC.finite_support y
  refine finiteVariableStage_map_mem_subring δ ι' T S g W hcoeff (fun j _ => hgen j) ?_ hS
  intro j _ n
  by_cases hp : T j ∈ positiveEvenPart Cᵢ
  · rw [← hgdpow n _ hp]
    exact hdpowgen j n
  · rw [δ.dpow_null hp, map_zero]
    exact Subring.zero_mem _

end StageUnion

section TowerMap

attribute [local instance] GradedDPAlgebra.ring GradedDPAlgebra.algebra
  GradedDPAlgebra.graded GradedDPAlgebra.strict

attribute [local instance] gradedLimitGradedAlgebra gradedLimitStrictlyGradedComm

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (A₀ : GradedDPAlgebra.{u, max u v z} R) (Jdx : ℕ → Type v)

/-- **The universal property of the colimit of the `ω`-tower, with the target universe free.**
A morphism out of the base together with a homogeneous value of degree `n + 1` for each variable
of degree `n + 1` extends to a morphism out of the colimit, for a target in *any* universe.

`DividedPowers.TateResolution.towerColimit_existsUnique_lift` says the same for a target in the
single universe that was fixed when the stages of the tower were chosen. The extra generality is
what lets the colimit be mapped into an algebra built out of its own carrier, which is how the
freeness of the colimit over its base is established. -/
public theorem towerColimit_exists_gradedDPHom (E : GradedDPAlgebra.{u, y} R)
    (g : GradedDPHom A₀ E) (t : (n : ℕ) → Jdx n → E.carrier)
    (ht : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : Jdx n), t n j ∈ E.grade (n + 1)) :
    ∃ F : GradedDPHom (towerColimit A₀ Jdx) E,
      (∀ a : A₀.carrier, F.hom ((towerCoefficient A₀ Jdx).hom a) = g.hom a) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (j : Jdx n), F.hom (towerVariable A₀ Jdx n j) = t n j) := by
  classical
  -- One step of the tower, by the mapping property of a set-variable extension.
  have hstep : ∀ (k : ℕ) (Gk : GradedDPHom (towerStage A₀ Jdx k) E),
      ∃ Gk1 : GradedDPHom (towerStage A₀ Jdx (k + 1)) E,
        (∀ x : (towerStage A₀ Jdx k).carrier,
          Gk1.hom ((towerStep A₀ Jdx k).hom x) = Gk.hom x) ∧
        (∀ j : Jdx k, Gk1.hom (towerGenerator A₀ Jdx k j) = t k j) := by
    intro k Gk
    obtain ⟨g1, hg1, -⟩ := (towerStage_isSetVariableExtension A₀ Jdx k).existsUnique_ringHom
      E.grade E.gamma Gk.hom.toRingHom (t k) Gk.map_grade Gk.map_dpow (ht k)
    have hcomm : ∀ r : R, g1 (algebraMap R (towerStage A₀ Jdx (k + 1)).carrier r) =
        algebraMap R E.carrier r := by
      intro r
      rw [← (towerStep A₀ Jdx k).hom.commutes r, hg1.1]
      exact Gk.hom.commutes r
    exact ⟨⟨{ toRingHom := g1, commutes' := hcomm }, hg1.2.2.1, hg1.2.2.2⟩, hg1.1, hg1.2.1⟩
  choose stepHom hstepRestrict hstepGen using hstep
  let G : (n : ℕ) → GradedDPHom (towerStage A₀ Jdx n) E := fun n =>
    Nat.rec g (fun k Gk => stepHom k Gk) n
  obtain ⟨F, hF, -⟩ := chainColimit_existsUnique_lift (towerStage A₀ Jdx)
    (towerStep A₀ Jdx) E G fun k => hstepRestrict k (G k)
  exact ⟨F, hF 0, fun n j => (hF (n + 1) _).trans (hstepGen n (G n) j)⟩

/-- Every stage of the `ω`-tower maps into the union of the finite variable stages. -/
private theorem towerStage_mem_stageUnion (B : GradedDPAlgebra.{u, max u v z} R)
    (incl : (n : ℕ) → GradedDPHom (towerStage A₀ Jdx n) B) {K : ℕ → Type y}
    (TT : (Σ n : ℕ, K n) → B.carrier)
    (hTT : ∀ (n : ℕ) (k : Jdx n), ∃ j : Σ m : ℕ, K m,
      TT j = (incl (n + 1)).hom (towerGenerator A₀ Jdx n k))
    (hstep : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : (towerStage A₀ Jdx n).carrier),
      (incl (n + 1)).hom ((towerStep A₀ Jdx n).hom x) = (incl n).hom x) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (y : (towerStage A₀ Jdx n).carrier),
      (incl n).hom y ∈ variableStageUnion B.gamma (incl 0).hom TT := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro y
      exact coefficient_mem_variableStageUnion B.gamma (incl 0).hom TT y
  | succ n ih =>
      exact setVariableExtension_map_mem_subring
        (towerStage A₀ Jdx (n + 1)).gamma (towerGenerator A₀ Jdx n)
        (towerStage_isSetVariableExtension A₀ Jdx n) B.grade B.gamma
        (variableStageUnion B.gamma (incl 0).hom TT) (incl (n + 1)).hom
        (incl (n + 1)).map_dpow (fun a => by rw [hstep n a]; exact ih a)
        (fun k => by
          obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hTT n k
          exact hj ▸ generator_mem_variableStageUnion B.gamma (incl 0).hom TT j)
        (fun k m => by
          obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hTT n k
          exact hj ▸ dpow_generator_mem_variableStageUnion B.gamma (incl 0).hom TT j m)

/-- **The finite variable stages cover an algebra exhausted by the stages of the `ω`-tower.**
Stated for an abstract bundle rather than for `DividedPowers.TateResolution.towerColimit`: the
colimit's carrier is a reducible abbreviation for a `DirectLimit`, so instance search unfolds it
and every unification against a `Subring` of it becomes expensive. Proved here with the bundle a
variable, it is cheap to instantiate. -/
private theorem finite_support_of_tower (B : GradedDPAlgebra.{u, max u v z} R)
    (incl : (n : ℕ) → GradedDPHom (towerStage A₀ Jdx n) B) {K : ℕ → Type y}
    (TT : (Σ n : ℕ, K n) → B.carrier)
    (hTT : ∀ (n : ℕ) (k : Jdx n), ∃ j : Σ m : ℕ, K m,
      TT j = (incl (n + 1)).hom (towerGenerator A₀ Jdx n k))
    (hstep : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : (towerStage A₀ Jdx n).carrier),
      (incl (n + 1)).hom ((towerStep A₀ Jdx n).hom x) = (incl n).hom x)
    (hcover : ∀ x : B.carrier, ∃ (n : ℕ) (y : (towerStage A₀ Jdx n).carrier),
      (incl n).hom y = x)
    (x : B.carrier) :
    ∃ S : Finset (Σ n : ℕ, K n), x ∈ finiteVariableStage B.gamma (incl 0).hom TT S := by
  obtain ⟨n, y, hy⟩ := hcover x
  rw [← hy]
  exact towerStage_mem_stageUnion A₀ Jdx B incl TT hTT hstep n y

/-- **The finite variable stages cover the colimit of the `ω`-tower.** Every element comes from
some stage of the tower, and each stage is generated over the previous one by its variables and
their divided powers; a variable of odd degree has vanishing positive divided powers, which is
why those are accounted for by `dpow_null` rather than by transport along the inclusion. -/
public theorem towerColimit_finite_support {K : ℕ → Type y}
    (TT : (Σ n : ℕ, K n) → (towerColimit A₀ Jdx).carrier)
    (hTT : ∀ (n : ℕ) (k : Jdx n), ∃ j : Σ m : ℕ, K m, TT j = towerVariable A₀ Jdx n k)
    (x : (towerColimit A₀ Jdx).carrier) :
    ∃ S : Finset (Σ n : ℕ, K n),
      x ∈ finiteVariableStage (towerColimit A₀ Jdx).gamma (towerCoefficient A₀ Jdx).hom TT S :=
  finite_support_of_tower A₀ Jdx (towerColimit A₀ Jdx) (towerInclusion A₀ Jdx) TT hTT
    (chainColimitInclusion_step (towerStage A₀ Jdx) (towerStep A₀ Jdx))
    (chainColimit_exists_stage (towerStage A₀ Jdx) (towerStep A₀ Jdx)) x

end TowerMap

section LiftMap

attribute [local instance] GradedDPAlgebra.ring GradedDPAlgebra.algebra
  GradedDPAlgebra.graded GradedDPAlgebra.strict

attribute [local instance] gradedLimitGradedAlgebra gradedLimitStrictlyGradedComm

variable {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {σ : Type z}
  [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
  {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
  {γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜} {ι : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] A}
  (hpoly : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial 𝒜 γ ι)

/-- **The lifted algebra of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/SquareZeroLiftData.lean` is free on its
coefficients and its variables, over targets in its own universe.** An `R'`-algebra morphism out
of `R'[xᵢ]` landing in degree zero, together with a homogeneous value of degree `n + 1` for each
variable of degree `n + 1`, extends to a morphism of graded divided power algebras out of `B`.

`DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftHom_spec` gives this only for targets whose carrier lies in the
universe of `A`, which excludes every algebra built from `B`'s own carrier; here the target may be
anywhere in the universe `max u v w z` in which `B` itself lives. That is what the freeness
arguments for `B` need: they test an element of `B` against an algebra constructed out of a
subring of `B`. -/
public theorem liftAlgebra_exists_gradedDPHom (E : GradedDPAlgebra.{u, max u v w z} R')
    (fP : MvPolynomial σ R' →ₐ[R'] E.carrier) (hfP : ∀ p, fP p ∈ E.grade 0)
    (t : (n : ℕ) → hpoly.indices n → E.carrier)
    (ht : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n), t n j ∈ E.grade (n + 1)) :
    ∃ F : GradedDPHom (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly) E,
      (∀ p : MvPolynomial σ R', F.hom ((liftCoefficientHom (R' := R') hpoly).hom
          ((liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A).symm p)) = fP p) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n), F.hom (liftVariable (R' := R') hpoly n j) = t n j) := by
  classical
  let g : GradedDPHom (liftBase R' σ R A) E :=
    degreeZeroDPHom R' (ULift.{max u v w z} (MvPolynomial σ R')) E
      (fP.comp (liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A).toAlgHom)
      (fun p => hfP ((liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A) p))
  obtain ⟨F, hF1, hF2⟩ :
      ∃ F : GradedDPHom (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly) E,
        (∀ a : (liftBase R' σ R A).carrier,
            F.hom ((liftCoefficientHom (R' := R') hpoly).hom a) = g.hom a) ∧
          (∀ (n : ℕ) (j : liftIndex hpoly n),
            F.hom (liftVariable (R' := R') hpoly n j.down) = t n j.down) :=
    towerColimit_exists_gradedDPHom (liftBase R' σ R A) (liftIndex hpoly) E
      g (fun n j => t n j.down) (fun n j => ht n j.down)
  refine ⟨F, fun p => ?_, fun n j => hF2 n (ULift.up j)⟩
  rw [hF1 ((liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A).symm p)]
  show fP ((liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A) ((liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A).symm p)) = fP p
  rw [AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

end LiftMap

end DividedPowers.TateResolution

